cmd/dlv, pkg/gobuild, pkg/proc: start the program with exactly dlv's environment

A program dlv exec started had variables dlv was not given, and a
program that does more or less work for another environment, as the Go
runtime does when it first reads it, runs differently: a
GOEXPERIMENT=detsched program runs another schedule, so a replay under
Delve was not the replay.

  - CGO_CFLAGS=-O0 -g, on every platform: dlv set it in its own
    environment, for the Cgo code of the builds of dlv debug and dlv
    test, and the program inherited it. It is now set only in the
    environment of those builds, when it is not set already.
  - PWD, on Linux: os/exec adds PWD=DIR when a command has a Dir and no
    Env, and the native backend set Dir to the working directory. It
    now sets Env, as lldb-server's launch does.
  - __CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING, on macOS: debugserver, started with the
    program on its command line, adds its own environment to the
    program's, -e or not, and CoreFoundation has added that variable to
    debugserver's. debugserver is now started without the program, which
    it launches at the A packet, after Delve connects, with exactly the
    environment its -e options give; the stdio paths, -D and
    --unmask-signals apply as before.

On macOS Delve also appends asyncpreemptoff=1 to a GODEBUG the
environment has, which it keeps for other programs; a detsched program,
which preempts only at ticks, never with signals, gets its GODEBUG
unchanged (proc.IsDetschedExecutable reads its symbol table before it
runs).

The environment is a generic fix for upstream Delve; GODEBUG is
detsched's (0003).

